-- title:
--   Every finite idèle class arises as a kernel ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$ that is algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$, and let $X_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with invertible discriminant such that the only point $P$ of the affine model of $X_0$ with $q' \cdot P = 0$ is $0$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a < 0$, $b < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q' \in v$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is an order (containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated, with $\mathbb{Q}$-span everything) and is maximal among orders containing it, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring `rationalEndSubring` of $\operatorname{End}$ of the points of $X_0$ base-changed to $\kappa$ — the subring generated by those additive endomorphisms which are zero or given by rational functions outside a finite set of $x$-coordinates — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$, with image exactly $\Lambda$. Then for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ there exist a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\kappa$ with invertible discriminant, a nonzero additive map $\chi$ from the points of $X_0$ to the points of $W$ over $\kappa$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$, such that the $\theta$-image of the kernel ideal $\{\alpha \mid \alpha = \rho \circ \chi \text{ for some } \rho \in \mathrm{rationalHomSet}(W, X_0)\}$ equals the image under quaternion conjugation of $d \cdot (\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b] \cap x\widehat{\Lambda})$, where the latter lattice is [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda$ $x$, the elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$ whose image in the adelic algebra lies in $x$ times the subgroup generated by $z \otimes \alpha$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adèle.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the Deuring correspondence at level one: every ideal class of the maximal order $\Lambda = \theta(\operatorname{End} X_0)$, presented by a finite idèle $x$, is realised as the kernel ideal of an isogeny out of the supersingular curve $X_0$. It is used to build the bijection between the class set of $\Lambda$ and the supersingular curves over $\kappa$, and in the analysis of kernel ideals attached to intersections of conjugated lattices.
